{"id":"twitter:1947324879709020521","tweet_id":"1947324879709020521","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1947324879709020521","title":"Here is the link to the article. https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022103121000871 Need to dig into their methodology of methodo","summary":"Here is the link to the article. https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022103121000871 Need to dig into their methodology of methodological literacy more. It is good to see the use of replication studies to scale, but the models shifted slightly so it was more a formative design rater than replication","date":"2025-07-21","published":"2025-07-21T15:56:45+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947324171471507929","reply_tweet_id":"1947324171471507929","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Here is the link to the article. <a href=\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022103121000871\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022103121000871</a><br><br>Need to dig into their methodology of methodological literacy more. <br><br>It is good to see the use of replication studies to scale, but the models shifted slightly so it was more a formative design rater than replication</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947324879709020521","display_date":"July 21, 2025 · 15:56 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1947324171471507929","tweet_id":"1947324171471507929","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1947324171471507929","title":"The authors conclude, \"trust in science can leave people vulnerable to believing in pseudoscience\" I am not sure I agree with that sentiment per se. T","summary":"The authors conclude, \"trust in science can leave people vulnerable to believing in pseudoscience\" I am not sure I agree with that sentiment per se. The models did have a ton of interactions. There are some ecological validity issues as well in my opinion.","date":"2025-07-21","published":"2025-07-21T15:53:56+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947323306819891618","reply_tweet_id":"1947323306819891618","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>The authors conclude, &quot;trust in science can leave people vulnerable to believing in pseudoscience&quot;<br><br>I am not sure I agree with that sentiment per se. The models did have a ton of interactions.<br><br>There are some ecological validity issues as well in my opinion.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947324171471507929","display_date":"July 21, 2025 · 15:53 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
