{"id":"twitter:1947319309258158591","tweet_id":"1947319309258158591","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1947319309258158591","title":"ANCOVA compares means of different groups on a dependent variable while controlling for the effect of a continuous covariates You assume covariate and","summary":"ANCOVA compares means of different groups on a dependent variable while controlling for the effect of a continuous covariates You assume covariate and the dependent variable is the same for all groups, but sometimes, often that assumption is violated. pre-tests good example","date":"2025-07-21","published":"2025-07-21T15:34:37+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947318652912505315","reply_tweet_id":"1947318652912505315","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>ANCOVA  compares  means of different groups on a dependent variable while controlling for  the effect of a continuous covariates<br><br>You assume covariate and the dependent variable is the same for all groups, but sometimes, often that assumption is violated.<br><br>pre-tests good example</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1947319309258158591","display_date":"July 21, 2025 · 15:34 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
