{"id":"twitter:1946587726758756435","tweet_id":"1946587726758756435","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1946587726758756435","title":"@IAMERICAbooted and people who pay for fancy policy packs don't realize they already license a compliant solution with Purview and Azure Policy https:","summary":"@IAMERICAbooted and people who pay for fancy policy packs don't realize they already license a compliant solution with Purview and Azure Policy https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/samples/gov-cmmc-l3 but often the policy and procedure writing drives the SSP writing, so there are secondary benefits (unless you find/replace)","date":"2025-07-19","published":"2025-07-19T15:07:34+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1946583240640229418","reply_tweet_id":"1946583240640229418","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@IAMERICAbooted and people who pay for fancy policy packs don&#x27;t realize they already license a compliant solution with Purview and Azure Policy<br><br><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/samples/gov-cmmc-l3\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/samples/gov-cmmc-l3</a><br><br>but often the policy and procedure writing drives the SSP writing, so there are secondary benefits<br><br>(unless you find/replace)</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1946587726758756435","display_date":"July 19, 2025 · 15:07 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
