{"id":"twitter:1945102386638225498","tweet_id":"1945102386638225498","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1945102386638225498","title":"@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO Here is the data source: https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/piaac/skillsmap/src/PDF/STATE.pdf So what state is worse ","summary":"@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO Here is the data source: https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/piaac/skillsmap/src/PDF/STATE.pdf So what state is worse is dependant on if you choose 1. Lowest average score 2. % of adults below level 1 Basic But the data is from the same report","date":"2025-07-15","published":"2025-07-15T12:45:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1945101806729654669","reply_tweet_id":"1945101806729654669","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO Here is the data source: <a href=\"https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/piaac/skillsmap/src/PDF/STATE.pdf\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://nces.ed.gov/surveys/piaac/skillsmap/src/PDF/STATE.pdf</a><br><br>So what state is worse is dependant on if you choose<br>1. Lowest average score<br>2. % of adults below level 1 Basic<br><br>But the data is from the same report</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1945102386638225498","display_date":"July 15, 2025 · 12:45 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1945101806729654669","tweet_id":"1945101806729654669","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1945101806729654669","title":"@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO My apologies. Public Policy Institute of California is using the NCES numbers. yes with those metrics Californ","summary":"@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO My apologies. Public Policy Institute of California is using the NCES numbers. yes with those metrics California and New York are 1 and 2 Followed by Texas and Florida it has more to do with English not being a first language not a red or blue state https://t.co/bStJxkysQV","date":"2025-07-15","published":"2025-07-15T12:43:03+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/Necro_304Mav/status/1945100584287076803","reply_tweet_id":"1945100584287076803","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Necro_304Mav @TifaAuntie @FredFellaIMO My apologies. Public Policy Institute of California is using the NCES numbers. yes with those metrics California and New York are 1 and 2<br><br>Followed by Texas and Florida<br><br>it has more to do with English not being a first language not a red or blue state <a href=\"https://t.co/bStJxkysQV\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/bStJxkysQV</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/b16d67e6e1169f17103ad0acd29716ab.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1945101806729654669","display_date":"July 15, 2025 · 12:43 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/b16d67e6e1169f17103ad0acd29716ab.jpg"]}
