{"id":"twitter:1944555789273739750","tweet_id":"1944555789273739750","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1944555789273739750","title":"Gee came up with six rules on how we define words and thus ourselves in the negotiation of the world https://t.co/is08NO5NfX","summary":"Gee came up with six rules on how we define words and thus ourselves in the negotiation of the world https://t.co/is08NO5NfX","date":"2025-07-14","published":"2025-07-14T00:33:22+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944552304067395630","reply_tweet_id":"1944552304067395630","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Gee came up with six rules on how we define words and thus ourselves in the negotiation of the world <a href=\"https://t.co/is08NO5NfX\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/is08NO5NfX</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/d1a954c4bb53a3371e0e982876dabf4c.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944555789273739750","display_date":"July 14, 2025 · 00:33 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/d1a954c4bb53a3371e0e982876dabf4c.jpg"]}
{"id":"twitter:1944552304067395630","tweet_id":"1944552304067395630","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1944552304067395630","title":"Which means we have to draw on Foucault and think about the power relations in the negotiation of meaning of the self. Meaning is always rooted in neg","summary":"Which means we have to draw on Foucault and think about the power relations in the negotiation of meaning of the self. Meaning is always rooted in negotation of social practice Definitions do not exist in nature. They are tools of mediated practice. https://t.co/fov6HtmqpA","date":"2025-07-14","published":"2025-07-14T00:19:31+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944550368492581123","reply_tweet_id":"1944550368492581123","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Which means we have to draw on Foucault and think about the power relations in the negotiation of meaning of the self.<br><br>Meaning is always rooted in negotation of social practice<br><br>Definitions do not exist in nature. They are tools of mediated practice. <a href=\"https://t.co/fov6HtmqpA\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/fov6HtmqpA</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/30eeda348e49f9424f1b54a905c33ff7.png\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944552304067395630","display_date":"July 14, 2025 · 00:19 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/30eeda348e49f9424f1b54a905c33ff7.png"]}
{"id":"twitter:1944550368492581123","tweet_id":"1944550368492581123","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1944550368492581123","title":"Under this perspective Words do not have fixed definitions. Words and identity are driven by knowledge and beliefs and get built by stories and cultur","summary":"Under this perspective Words do not have fixed definitions. Words and identity are driven by knowledge and beliefs and get built by stories and cultural models. Not definitions (Gee, 1990) https://t.co/RMlOTmD5Ny","date":"2025-07-14","published":"2025-07-14T00:11:50+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944547948081156427","reply_tweet_id":"1944547948081156427","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Under this perspective Words do not have fixed definitions. <br><br>Words and identity are driven by  knowledge and beliefs and  get built by stories and cultural models.<br><br>Not definitions<br><br>(Gee, 1990) <a href=\"https://t.co/RMlOTmD5Ny\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/RMlOTmD5Ny</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/2681cd8f331608dbaa989e78653c59da.png\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944550368492581123","display_date":"July 14, 2025 · 00:11 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/2681cd8f331608dbaa989e78653c59da.png"]}
{"id":"twitter:1944547948081156427","tweet_id":"1944547948081156427","source":"twitter","type":"photos","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1944547948081156427","title":"Covering Identity in our Digital Teaching and Learning class Could teach entire semester on construct of self mediated by digital texts One area my st","summary":"Covering Identity in our Digital Teaching and Learning class Could teach entire semester on construct of self mediated by digital texts One area my students struggle with is the idea of a mediated environment found in Vygotsky and Bakhtin Hoping infographic helps https://t.co/M5blFc2dA2","date":"2025-07-14","published":"2025-07-14T00:02:13+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Covering Identity  in our Digital Teaching and Learning class<br><br>Could teach entire semester on construct of self mediated by digital texts<br><br>One area my students struggle with is the idea of a mediated environment found in Vygotsky and Bakhtin<br><br>Hoping infographic helps <a href=\"https://t.co/M5blFc2dA2\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/M5blFc2dA2</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/b6bb75088be5e0531468f2692505f10c.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1944547948081156427","display_date":"July 14, 2025 · 00:02 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/b6bb75088be5e0531468f2692505f10c.jpg"]}
