{"id":"twitter:1942221902853935415","tweet_id":"1942221902853935415","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1942221902853935415","title":"To address 3.7 trillion in new debt through growth alone you would need 21 trillion in GDP growth over a decade. That means averaging 5% GDP growth pe","summary":"To address 3.7 trillion in new debt through growth alone you would need 21 trillion in GDP growth over a decade. That means averaging 5% GDP growth per quarter for ten years. @SecScottBessent knows that is impossible. https://x.com/stonecold603/status/1942220114704654585","date":"2025-07-07","published":"2025-07-07T13:59:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>To address 3.7 trillion in new debt through growth alone you would need 21 trillion in GDP growth over a decade.<br><br>That means averaging 5% GDP growth per quarter for ten years.<br><br>@SecScottBessent knows that is impossible. <a href=\"https://x.com/stonecold603/status/1942220114704654585\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/stonecold603/status/1942220114704654585</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1942221902853935415","display_date":"July 07, 2025 · 13:59 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
