{"id":"twitter:1939764260948914189","tweet_id":"1939764260948914189","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1939764260948914189","title":"What if you could use actual math? To cover the 3.3 trillion added to the debt we would need about 21 trillion in GDP growth. That works out to bout 5","summary":"What if you could use actual math? To cover the 3.3 trillion added to the debt we would need about 21 trillion in GDP growth. That works out to bout 5% average growth every quarter, for a decade That is a mathematical impssobility https://x.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1939742277686964474","date":"2025-06-30","published":"2025-06-30T19:13:33+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>What if you could use actual math?<br><br>To cover the 3.3 trillion added to the debt we would need about 21 trillion in GDP growth.<br><br>That works out to bout 5% average growth every quarter, for a decade<br><br>That is a mathematical impssobility <a href=\"https://x.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1939742277686964474\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1939742277686964474</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1939764260948914189","display_date":"June 30, 2025 · 19:13 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
