{"id":"twitter:1936050831280812489","tweet_id":"1936050831280812489","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1936050831280812489","title":"@IceSolst Research in cognitive science disagrees. All of those techniques have been shown to lead to higher retention in learners. I think the mistak","summary":"@IceSolst Research in cognitive science disagrees. All of those techniques have been shown to lead to higher retention in learners. I think the mistake occurs when authors mix up their purpose. Do you want to teach or market? Good teaching is great marketing, not reciprocal","date":"2025-06-20","published":"2025-06-20T13:17:42+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/IceSolst/status/1936047880675934212","reply_tweet_id":"1936047880675934212","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@IceSolst Research in cognitive science disagrees. All of those techniques have been shown to lead to higher retention in learners.<br><br>I think the mistake occurs when authors mix up their purpose. Do you want to teach or market? <br><br>Good teaching is great marketing, not reciprocal</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1936050831280812489","display_date":"June 20, 2025 · 13:17 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
